<http://data.silknow.org/object/7002ad3c-ed59-3f00-b78b-855d3813436f/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dress fabric of warp-faced silk brocaded with silk and metal thread impressed with lines; piced.\n\nExtensively pieced. The seams are easily seen from the back. There seems to be hardly any distortion to the pattern. In larger pieces impressed lines can be clearly seen: four lines form a lozenge around the motifs. The motif has a bird perched on a stem with 2 buds and one blossom. The birds face to the left on the bottom row and to the right on the top row. The silk appears to be floss [untwisted]. The leaves are green, the flowers are white and 2 shades of pink. The birds are also 2 shades of pink and white. There are traces of metal thread which is silver-gilt strip open S-wound on a pink silk core."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/7002ad3c-ed59-3f00-b78b-855d3813436f> .

